INTERPRETATION
The full-prefix kernel is not a theorem for arbitrary undirected graphs,
for rooted graphs whose root is a leaf, for graphs with reflected roots,
or even for graphs with a reflection exchanging two leaves.  Thus a proof
cannot use only symmetry, nonnegative adjacency, and the unique boundary
edge.  No counterexample occurred among the 527 connected reflected,
row-convex, endpoint-leaf graphs of order at most nine encountered in the
34,673,238-mask exhaustive enumeration, through prefix 50.  Row-convexity
is the additional structure present in the SU(2) fusion intervals, but the
bounded pass is only route-selection evidence.

